  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compute the difference between each outcome and a reference value (zero in this case), then consider the weighted differences (i.e., expected values), and prefer the lottery with the more favorable mean difference. In this case, both lotteries have the same expected value (6 Euros), so the mean difference is equal, and the reason would be indifferent. However, the verbal report does not mention any calculation of expected values, differences from a reference, or any comparison of weighted differences. Instead, the individual expresses a subjective feeling of indifference due to the vanishingly small probabilities and makes a choice based on that feeling. There is no indication that they applied the rule involving differences and probabilities. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The individual did not engage with the formal rule of the decision reason, even though the problem is mathematically compatible with it.",
